# Form rendering

Use `RenderViews::buildForm()` for new forms and when touching an existing form. Do not assemble forms with `buildStartForm()`, `buildFormFieldsGrid()`, or `buildEndFormWithButtons()` unless you are only patching a file that has not been migrated yet.

`RenderViews` is a facade. Add form markup in `src/Html/Form.php`, cards and lists in `src/Html/Blocks.php`, and page rendering in `src/Http/View.php`. Do not add new behavior to `RenderViews`. List behavior belongs in `layouts/js/app.js` behind a data attribute. Class names stay aligned with `layouts/css/base.css`.

A new plain field type is `FieldControl::register($type, $render)`. Menus stay in the item screen. An application wording prefix is `Wording::register($controllerPrefix, $constantPrefix)`.

Do not set the `HEADING` constant. Pass the card title as the first argument to `buildForm()`. Do not use `buildFormSectionHeading()`.

## Pattern

1. Build `$fields` as `label => RenderViews::build*()` HTML.
2. Build `$buttons` with `RenderViews::buildFormButton()`.
3. Call `buildForm($title, $actionUrl, $fields, $buttons)`.
4. `define('BODY_CONTENT', $html)` then `RenderViews::renderThemePage('main_page_content', SET_THEME)`.

`buildForm()` returns HTML. It does not set `BODY_CONTENT`.

Hidden fields use an empty label: `$fields[''] = RenderViews::buildHiddenInput(...)`.

Field helpers: `buildTextInput`, `buildTextArea`, `buildSelectDropdown`, `buildPasswordInput`, `buildCheckBox`, `buildRadioButton`, `buildHiddenInput`, `buildFileInput`, `buildDateInputFields`.

## Exemplar

`showSearchOptions()` in `app/Http/Controllers/administration_item_settings.php`.

Same shape: `showUserGroupSearch()` in `administration_security.php`, `showactionPackages()` in `administration_actions.php`.
